  "schoolyard": 1,
  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree is great for learning about leaf morphology and variation, ethnobotany, and ecology.  The shiny, green leaves also vary widely in shape within one tree and among many trees; some are more deeply lobed while others may be entire. The acorns and acorn cupules are great materials for natural art projects. The tree is an important food resource and habitat for mammals and birds. Deer often browse the young growth.&nbsp;",
